+# 01: Place a Hold and see the queue
+
+**Spec:** `.scratch/holds/spec.md`
+
+**What to build:** When every copy of a Title is out, a member can place a Hold on it, and staff can see the Hold queue. `LendingService.place_hold(member_id, isbn) -> Hold` creates a Waiting Hold. `LendingService.holds_for(isbn) -> list[Hold]` lists the Title's active (Waiting and Ready) Holds, first in line first.
+
+The models gain a dataclass `Hold(hold_id, member_id, isbn, placed_on, status, copy_id, pickup_by)` and an enum `HoldStatus` with `WAITING`, `READY`, `FULFILLED`, `CANCELLED` and `EXPIRED`. Values are lowercase strings, like the other enums. A new Hold is `WAITING`, dated today from the Clock, with `copy_id` and `pickup_by` both `None`. Hold ids come from the repository's sequence with prefix `H` (`H0001`, …). The repository gains storage for Holds in its existing style. `Hold` and `HoldStatus` are exported from the package.
+
+`place_hold` runs its checks in this order, so the money conversation comes first as it does at checkout:
+
+1. Member lookup (`MemberNotFound`).
+2. The hold block: `AccountBlocked(member_id, balance, 5.00)` when the Balance is ≥ 5.00. The 5.00 hold threshold lives in the circulation policy next to the borrowing threshold, and it is the same for every member category.
+3. Title lookup (`TitleNotFound`).
+4. A new `HoldNotAllowed(LendingError)`, with a readable message saying why, when any of these is true:
+   - the Title has no copy that isn't withdrawn;
+   - any copy of the Title is `AVAILABLE`;
+   - the member already has a Waiting or Ready Hold on the Title;
+   - the member has an open Loan on a copy of the Title.
+
+There is no limit on how many Holds a member can have. A member who becomes Blocked after placing a Hold keeps their place.
+
+`holds_for` raises `TitleNotFound` for an unknown ISBN. Otherwise it returns the Holds in placement order: the order they were created, not `placed_on`. Holds placed on the same day therefore keep their order.
+
+**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately)
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] With `D1` checked out, `place_hold` returns a `WAITING` Hold for that member and `dvd-1`, dated today, with no `copy_id` and no `pickup_by`.
+- [ ] Two members placing Holds on `dvd-1` on the same day appear in `holds_for` in the order they were placed. A third placed the next day comes last.
+- [ ] `holds_for` on a Title nobody is waiting for returns `[]`. An unknown ISBN raises `TitleNotFound`.
+- [ ] `HoldNotAllowed` when a copy of the Title is `AVAILABLE`. For example, `978-1` with only `B1` checked out still has `B2` on the shelf.
+- [ ] `HoldNotAllowed` for a Title with no copies, and for a Title whose only copies are all withdrawn.
+- [ ] `HoldNotAllowed` when the member already has a Waiting Hold on the Title.
+- [ ] `HoldNotAllowed` when the member has the Title on loan.
+- [ ] `AccountBlocked` from `place_hold` at a Balance of exactly 5.00 and above, carrying the member, the Balance and a threshold of 5.00. A Balance of 4.99 can place a Hold.
+- [ ] A child is Blocked from Holds at the same 5.00, through Manual charges.
+- [ ] An unknown member gets `MemberNotFound`. A Blocked member asking for an unknown ISBN gets `AccountBlocked`. An unknown ISBN otherwise gets `TitleNotFound`.
+- [ ] A member whose Balance rises to 5.00 or more after placing a Hold keeps it in `holds_for`, in the same position.
+- [ ] Tests drive only the public `LendingService` interface with the shared fixtures and the `FixedClock`. Extra members are registered in the tests themselves.
+- [ ] The README's Concepts section gains Hold and Hold queue, and its Blocked entry mentions the 5.00 hold threshold, consistent with `GLOSSARY.md`.
+- [ ] All existing tests still pass.
