+# 02: A returned copy goes to the Hold shelf
+
+**Spec:** `.scratch/holds/spec.md`
+
+**What to build:** A copy that comes back while someone is waiting for its Title is set aside for the first person in the queue, instead of going back on the shelf. `return_copy(copy_id)` keeps its signature and still returns the closed Loan. The Fine is posted exactly as today (ADR-0001), and only then is the copy placed.
+
+`CopyStatus` gains `ON_HOLD_SHELF` (value `"on_hold_shelf"`). Setting a copy aside is one rule, which later tickets reuse when a copy is freed by a cancellation or an expiry, or added to the catalogue:
+
+- If the Title has a Waiting Hold, the copy goes to `ON_HOLD_SHELF`. The first Waiting Hold in placement order then becomes `READY`, with that `copy_id` and a Pickup deadline counted from today.
+- Otherwise the copy goes to `AVAILABLE`, as today.
+
+The Pickup deadline is the day the Hold becomes Ready plus 7 calendar days. If that falls on a closed day, it moves to the next open day, using the existing open-day rule the same way due dates do. The 7-day pickup period lives in the circulation policy.
+
+A copy on the Hold shelf counts as out. It isn't in `available_copies`. `withdraw_copy` still accepts only `AVAILABLE` copies, so it raises `CopyNotAvailable` for a copy on the Hold shelf. Another member can still place a Hold on a Title whose only copies are on the Hold shelf.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Place a Hold and see the queue).
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] `D1` checked out on Monday 2 March 2026, a Hold placed, and `D1` returned on Wednesday 4 March. `D1` is `ON_HOLD_SHELF`, and the Hold is `READY` with `copy_id` `D1` and `pickup_by` Wednesday 11 March.
+- [ ] A copy returned on Sunday 8 March makes a Hold Ready with `pickup_by` Monday 16 March, because Sunday 15 March is closed.
+- [ ] With two Holds waiting, only the first becomes Ready. The second stays `WAITING`, and `holds_for` lists the Ready Hold first.
+- [ ] With `B1` and `B2` both out and two Holds on `978-1`, each returned copy goes to the next Hold in placement order. This includes two Holds placed on the same day.
+- [ ] `return_copy` still returns the same closed Loan, and a late return still posts its Fine.
+- [ ] A return with nobody waiting shelves the copy as `AVAILABLE`, as before.
+- [ ] A copy on the Hold shelf isn't in `available_copies`. `withdraw_copy` on it raises `CopyNotAvailable`.
+- [ ] A member can place a Hold on a Title whose only copy is on the Hold shelf for someone else.
+- [ ] Tests drive only the public `LendingService` interface with the shared fixtures and the `FixedClock`. They don't call policy functions directly.
+- [ ] The README's Concepts section gains Hold shelf and Pickup deadline, and its Copy entry mentions `ON_HOLD_SHELF`, consistent with `GLOSSARY.md`.
+- [ ] All existing tests still pass.
