+# 03: Collect a Ready Hold at checkout
+
+**Spec:** `.scratch/holds/spec.md`
+
+**What to build:** The member a copy is set aside for collects it with an ordinary checkout. `checkout(member_id, copy_id)` keeps its signature and its check order: member, borrowing block (10.00), copy lookup, availability, loan limit. Only the meaning of "available" changes. A copy can be lent if either:
+
+- it is `AVAILABLE`; or
+- it is `ON_HOLD_SHELF`, it is set aside for a Ready Hold belonging to this member, and that Hold's Pickup deadline is today or later.
+
+Anything else raises `CopyNotAvailable(copy_id, status)`, as today. On success the Loan is created as today, the copy goes `ON_LOAN`, and the Hold becomes `FULFILLED`. It keeps its `copy_id` and `pickup_by` and leaves `holds_for`.
+
+After the Pickup deadline, collecting is refused even if the daily job hasn't run yet. The Hold stays Ready until the job expires it (ticket 05). If the borrowing block or the loan limit refuses the checkout, the Hold stays Ready and the copy stays on the Hold shelf, so the member can pay or return something and still collect before the deadline.
+
+**Blocked by:** 02 (A returned copy goes to the Hold shelf).
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] The Hold's member checks out the set-aside copy. They get a normal Loan, the copy is `ON_LOAN`, the Hold is `FULFILLED`, and it no longer appears in `holds_for`.
+- [ ] Collecting works on the deadline day itself. For example, Ready on Wednesday 4 March 2026 and collected on Wednesday 11 March.
+- [ ] Collecting the day after the deadline, with the daily job not yet run, raises `CopyNotAvailable`. The Hold is still `READY` and the copy still `ON_HOLD_SHELF`.
+- [ ] Any other member checking out the set-aside copy gets `CopyNotAvailable`, and the Hold stays Ready.
+- [ ] A Hold member whose Balance is 10.00 gets `AccountBlocked` when collecting. The Hold stays `READY`, and after a Payment brings the Balance below 10.00 they can collect before the deadline.
+- [ ] A Hold member at their loan limit gets `LoanLimitReached` when collecting. The Hold stays `READY`, and after returning a copy they can collect before the deadline.
+- [ ] A fulfilled Hold keeps its `copy_id` and `pickup_by`.
+- [ ] If `cancel_hold` already exists (ticket 04), cancelling a Fulfilled Hold raises `HoldNotAllowed`. Otherwise ticket 04 adds this test.
+- [ ] Checking out an `AVAILABLE` copy works exactly as before.
+- [ ] Tests drive only the public `LendingService` interface with the shared fixtures and the `FixedClock`.
+- [ ] The README's Concepts section gains Collect, consistent with `GLOSSARY.md`.
+- [ ] All existing tests still pass.
