+# 04: Cancel a Hold
+
+**Spec:** `.scratch/holds/spec.md`
+
+**What to build:** A member can cancel a Hold they no longer need. `LendingService.cancel_hold(hold_id) -> Hold` returns the cancelled Hold.
+
+- An unknown id raises a new `HoldNotFound(LendingError)`, which carries the `hold_id` like `LoanNotFound` does.
+- Only Waiting and Ready Holds can be cancelled. A Hold in any other state (`FULFILLED`, `CANCELLED` or `EXPIRED`) raises `HoldNotAllowed`. The check is on the status, so it covers every finished state the same way.
+- A `WAITING` Hold becomes `CANCELLED` and leaves the queue.
+- A `READY` Hold becomes `CANCELLED`, and its copy passes on through the set-aside rule from ticket 02. The next Waiting Hold becomes Ready with a Pickup deadline counted from today. If nobody is waiting, the copy goes back to `AVAILABLE`.
+- A cancelled Hold keeps its `copy_id` and `pickup_by`, if it had them.
+- Cancelling has no money check and posts no Charge.
+
+**Blocked by:** 02 (A returned copy goes to the Hold shelf).
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] Cancelling a Waiting Hold returns it as `CANCELLED`, and it leaves `holds_for`. The Holds behind it move up.
+- [ ] Cancelling a Ready Hold with someone waiting behind it: the copy stays `ON_HOLD_SHELF`, and the next Hold becomes `READY` with that copy and a `pickup_by` 7 days from today (moved past a closed day).
+- [ ] Cancelling a Ready Hold with nobody waiting puts the copy back to `AVAILABLE`.
+- [ ] A cancelled Ready Hold still shows its `copy_id` and `pickup_by`.
+- [ ] Cancelling a Cancelled Hold raises `HoldNotAllowed`. If ticket 03 or 05 has already landed, cancelling a Fulfilled or an Expired Hold raises `HoldNotAllowed` too.
+- [ ] An unknown hold id raises `HoldNotFound`, carrying the id.
+- [ ] Cancelling a Hold leaves the member's Balance unchanged, and works for a member who is Blocked.
+- [ ] Tests drive only the public `LendingService` interface with the shared fixtures and the `FixedClock`.
+- [ ] All existing tests still pass.
