+# 05: Daily job expires uncollected Holds
+
+**Spec:** `.scratch/holds/spec.md`
+
+**What to build:** A daily job clears Holds that nobody collected, so set-aside copies don't sit on the Hold shelf forever. `LendingService.expire_holds() -> list[Hold]` works from today's date on the Clock:
+
+- Every `READY` Hold whose Pickup deadline is before today becomes `EXPIRED`. It keeps its `copy_id` and `pickup_by`.
+- Each expired Hold's copy then passes on through the set-aside rule from ticket 02. The next Waiting Hold on that Title becomes Ready with a Pickup deadline counted from today. If nobody is waiting, the copy goes back to `AVAILABLE`.
+- A Hold made Ready during the run has a deadline at least 7 days away, so it never expires in the same run.
+- The job returns the Holds it expired, in placement order, across all Titles. A second run on the same day returns `[]` and changes nothing.
+- After days when it didn't run, the job expires everything now past its deadline. Copies passed on get deadlines counted from the day it actually runs.
+- Waiting Holds never expire. Expiry posts no Charge, because no-show fees are out of scope.
+
+**Blocked by:** 02 (A returned copy goes to the Hold shelf).
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] A Hold Ready on Wednesday 4 March 2026 (deadline Wednesday 11 March) is not expired by a run on 11 March, which returns `[]`.
+- [ ] A run on Thursday 12 March returns that Hold as `EXPIRED`, still showing its `copy_id` and `pickup_by`. It leaves `holds_for`.
+- [ ] With another Hold waiting, the copy stays `ON_HOLD_SHELF`, and that Hold becomes `READY` with `pickup_by` Thursday 19 March.
+- [ ] With nobody waiting, the copy goes back to `AVAILABLE`.
+- [ ] A second run on the same day returns `[]` and changes no Hold or copy.
+- [ ] A run after several missed days expires every Ready Hold now past its deadline, on every Title. It returns them in placement order and passes each copy on with a deadline counted from the day of the run.
+- [ ] A Waiting Hold is never expired, however long it has waited.
+- [ ] Expiry leaves the member's Balance unchanged.
+- [ ] If `cancel_hold` already exists (ticket 04), cancelling an Expired Hold raises `HoldNotAllowed`. Otherwise ticket 04 adds this test.
+- [ ] Tests drive only the public `LendingService` interface with the shared fixtures and the `FixedClock`.
+- [ ] All existing tests still pass.
