+# Holds
+
+Status: ready-for-agent
+
+## Problem Statement
+
+When every copy of a Title is out, a member who wants it has nothing to do but keep asking at the desk. Nothing records who asked first. When a copy comes back it goes straight onto the shelf, and whoever happens to be standing there takes it. The members who have been waiting longest get no priority. Staff have no list of who is waiting for what.
+
+## Solution
+
+A member can place a **Hold** on a Title when no copy of it is on the shelf. Holds on a Title form a **Hold queue** in the order they were placed. When a copy comes back, or a new copy is added, it doesn't go to the shelf. It is set aside on the **Hold shelf** for the first Waiting Hold, which becomes Ready. That member has until the **Pickup deadline**, seven days later (moved to the next open day if the library is closed), to **Collect** it. A member can cancel a Hold at any time before it is fulfilled. A daily job expires Ready Holds that nobody collected and passes each copy on to the next person waiting.
+
+Members who owe 5.00 or more are Blocked from placing Holds, which is lower than the 10.00 that blocks borrowing. Expiry costs nothing for now.
+
+Vocabulary follows `GLOSSARY.md` (see its Holds section). ADR-0001 is not changed by this feature.
+
+## User Stories
+
+1. As a member, I want to place a Hold on a Title when every copy is out, so that I don't have to keep asking at the desk.
+2. As a member, I want my Hold to be on the Title, not on a particular Copy, so that whichever copy comes back first can be mine.
+3. As a member, I want Holds served in the order they were placed, so that the people who have waited longest get the next copy.
+4. As a member who placed a Hold on the same day as someone else, I want the one placed first to stay first, so that the order is fair within a day as well.
+5. As a front-desk staff member, I want a Hold to be refused when a copy of the Title is on the shelf, so that the member just takes that copy.
+6. As a front-desk staff member, I want copies set aside for other members to count as out, so that a member can still queue for a Title whose only copies are on the Hold shelf.
+7. As a library manager, I want a Hold to be refused for a Title with no copies in circulation (none at all, or all withdrawn), so that nobody waits for a copy that will never come back.
+8. As a front-desk staff member, I want a member to be refused a second active Hold on the same Title, so that one member can't take two places in the queue.
+9. As a front-desk staff member, I want a member to be refused a Hold on a Title they already have a copy of on loan, so that nobody queues for something they already have.
+10. As a library manager, I want a member who owes 5.00 or more to be unable to place a Hold, so that members settle what they owe before claiming copies ahead of others.
+11. As a member who owes 4.99, I want to still be able to place a Hold, so that the block applies only at the threshold.
+12. As a library manager, I want the same 5.00 hold threshold for adults and children, so that there is one rule for Holds.
+13. As a front-desk staff member, I want a member Blocked for Holds to be told about the block before anything about the Title, so that we talk about the money first, as we do at checkout.
+14. As a developer calling the service, I want the hold block to raise the same error as the borrowing block, carrying the member, their Balance and the 5.00 threshold, so that the desk shows the same kind of message for both.
+15. As a member whose Balance rises after I placed a Hold, I want my Hold to keep its place in the queue, so that owing money later doesn't lose me my turn.
+16. As a member, I want there to be no limit on how many Holds I can have, so that I can queue for everything I want.
+17. As a front-desk staff member, I want a returned copy to go to the Hold shelf when someone is waiting for its Title, so that it doesn't end up back on the shelf for anyone to take.
+18. As a front-desk staff member, I want returning a copy to work exactly as before (same call, same closed Loan handed back, same Fine), so that the desk workflow doesn't change.
+19. As a member at the front of the queue, I want my Hold to become Ready with the copy set aside for me, so that I know which copy is mine.
+20. As a member with a Ready Hold, I want seven days to collect it, so that I have time to get to the library.
+21. As a member, I want a Pickup deadline that would land on a Sunday to move to the Monday, so that my last day to collect is a day the library is open.
+22. As a member, I want to be able to collect on the deadline day itself, so that "by Wednesday" means Wednesday is still fine.
+23. As a front-desk staff member, I want a new copy added to a Title that people are waiting for to go straight to the first person in the queue, so that nobody can take a new copy ahead of the queue.
+24. As a member with a Ready Hold, I want to collect my copy with an ordinary checkout, so that collecting works like any other loan.
+25. As a member, I want collecting my copy to fulfil my Hold, so that it leaves the queue.
+26. As a front-desk staff member, I want a copy on the Hold shelf to be refused to anyone but the member it is set aside for, so that a set-aside copy is never lent to someone else.
+27. As a member with a Ready Hold who now owes 10.00 or more, I want to be told I'm Blocked when I try to collect, and to keep my Hold until the deadline, so that I can pay and still collect in time.
+28. As a member with a Ready Hold who is at my loan limit, I want to be told about the limit when I try to collect, and to keep my Hold until the deadline, so that I can return something and still collect in time.
+29. As a member, I want to cancel a Hold I no longer need, whether it is Waiting or Ready, so that I don't keep a place I won't use.
+30. As the next member in the queue, I want a copy freed by a cancelled Ready Hold to pass to me straight away, with my own full seven days, so that I don't wait for the daily job.
+31. As a front-desk staff member, I want a copy freed by a cancellation to go back to the shelf when nobody else is waiting, so that it can be borrowed.
+32. As a developer calling the service, I want cancelling a Hold that is already fulfilled, cancelled or expired to be refused, so that a finished Hold never changes again.
+33. As a developer calling the service, I want an unknown Hold id to raise a not-found error, so that error handling matches the rest of the service.
+34. As a library manager, I want a daily job that expires Ready Holds whose Pickup deadline has passed, so that uncollected copies don't sit on the Hold shelf forever.
+35. As the next member in the queue, I want a copy freed by an expired Hold to pass to me, with seven days counted from the day the job runs, so that I get my full time to collect.
+36. As a front-desk staff member, I want a copy freed by an expired Hold to go back on the shelf when nobody else is waiting, so that it can be borrowed.
+37. As a library manager, I want the daily job to return the Holds it expired, so that staff can see whose copies were not collected.
+38. As a library manager, I want running the job twice on the same day to change nothing the second time, so that an accidental re-run is harmless.
+39. As a library manager, I want the job to catch up after days it didn't run, so that a missed day doesn't leave stale Holds behind.
+40. As a member with a Waiting Hold, I want it never to expire just from waiting, so that I keep my place however long the queue takes.
+41. As a member who misses a pickup, I want expiry to cost nothing, so that I'm not charged for changing my mind.
+42. As a front-desk staff member, I want to see the active Holds on a Title, first in line first, so that I can tell a member where they stand.
+43. As a front-desk staff member, I want a copy on the Hold shelf to be refused for withdrawal, so that a set-aside copy isn't taken out of circulation while someone is due to collect it.
+44. As a front-desk staff member, I want the list of available copies to leave out copies on the Hold shelf, so that I don't send a member to a copy that is set aside.
+45. As a developer calling the service, I want unknown members and Titles to raise the same not-found errors from the hold operations as everywhere else, so that error handling stays the same across the service.
+46. As a library manager, I want the hold threshold and the pickup period kept with the other circulation numbers, so that changing them is a one-line policy change.
+47. As a library manager, I want the Pickup deadline to follow the library's own closed-day rule, so that if we ever close on another weekday, deadlines move with due dates.
+
+## Implementation Decisions
+
+**Interface contract.** Other code will call exactly this, on `LendingService`:
+
+- `place_hold(member_id: str, isbn: str) -> Hold`: places a Waiting Hold.
+- `cancel_hold(hold_id: str) -> Hold`: cancels a Waiting or Ready Hold and returns it.
+- `expire_holds() -> list[Hold]`: the daily job. It returns the Holds it expired.
+- `holds_for(isbn: str) -> list[Hold]`: the active (Waiting and Ready) Holds on the Title, first in line first.
+- `return_copy(copy_id)` and `checkout(member_id, copy_id)` keep their signatures and return values. `add_copy` keeps its signature.
+
+**Models:**
+
+- A dataclass `Hold(hold_id: str, member_id: str, isbn: str, placed_on: date, status: HoldStatus, copy_id: str | None, pickup_by: date | None)`. It is mutable like `Loan`, and only the service changes it.
+- An enum `HoldStatus` with `WAITING`, `READY`, `FULFILLED`, `CANCELLED` and `EXPIRED`. Values are lowercase strings, as in the other enums.
+- `CopyStatus` gains `ON_HOLD_SHELF` (value `"on_hold_shelf"`).
+- A new Hold is `WAITING`, dated today from the Clock, with `copy_id` and `pickup_by` both `None`. They are set when it becomes `READY`. After that they are never cleared, so a Fulfilled, Cancelled or Expired Hold still shows the copy it had and its deadline.
+- Hold ids come from the repository's sequence with prefix `H` (`H0001`, `H0002`, …).
+- `Hold` and `HoldStatus` are exported from the package next to `Loan` and `CopyStatus`.
+
+**New errors**, both subclasses of `LendingError`:
+
+- `HoldNotAllowed`: a Hold can't be placed, or a Hold can't be cancelled in its current state. It has a readable message saying why.
+- `HoldNotFound`: carries the unknown `hold_id`, like `LoanNotFound`.
+- Existing errors are reused where they fit. That means `MemberNotFound`, `TitleNotFound`, `AccountBlocked` (with the 5.00 threshold), and `CopyNotAvailable` for a copy on the Hold shelf.
+
+**Policy:**
+
+- Hold threshold: 5.00, the same for every member category, next to the borrowing threshold.
+- Pickup period: 7 days. The Pickup deadline is the day the Hold becomes Ready plus 7 calendar days. If that falls on a closed day, it moves to the next open day, using the existing open-day rule the same way due dates do.
+- Worked examples (must hold): Ready on Wednesday 4 March 2026 gives a deadline of Wednesday 11 March. Ready on Sunday 8 March gives Sunday 15 March, which moves to Monday 16 March.
+
+**Placing a Hold.** Checks run in this order:
+
+1. Member lookup (`MemberNotFound`).
+2. The hold block: `AccountBlocked(member_id, balance, 5.00)` when the Balance is ≥ 5.00.
+3. Title lookup (`TitleNotFound`).
+4. `HoldNotAllowed` if any of these is true:
+   - the Title has no copy that isn't withdrawn;
+   - any copy of the Title is `AVAILABLE`;
+   - the member already has a Waiting or Ready Hold on the Title;
+   - the member has an open Loan on a copy of the Title.
+
+Copies `ON_LOAN` or `ON_HOLD_SHELF` both count as out. A member who becomes Blocked after placing a Hold keeps it. There is no limit on how many Holds a member can have.
+
+**Setting a copy aside.** One rule is used by every path that frees or adds a copy. If the Title has a Waiting Hold, the copy goes to `ON_HOLD_SHELF`. The first Waiting Hold in placement order then becomes `READY`, with this `copy_id` and a Pickup deadline counted from today. If no Hold is waiting, the copy goes to `AVAILABLE`. The rule is used by:
+
+- `return_copy`: the Loan is closed and its Fine posted exactly as today (ADR-0001), then the copy is set aside or shelved.
+- `add_copy`: a new copy of a Title with a Waiting Hold goes straight to the Hold shelf. The returned Copy shows `ON_HOLD_SHELF`.
+- `cancel_hold` of a Ready Hold, and `expire_holds`: the freed copy passes on, as described below.
+
+So an `AVAILABLE` copy and a Waiting Hold on the same Title never exist together.
+
+**Collecting.** The check order in `checkout` is unchanged: member, borrowing block (10.00), copy lookup, availability, loan limit. Availability now means one of two things:
+
+- the copy is `AVAILABLE`; or
+- the copy is `ON_HOLD_SHELF`, it is set aside for a Ready Hold belonging to this member, and that Hold's Pickup deadline is today or later.
+
+Anything else raises `CopyNotAvailable(copy_id, status)`. On success the Loan is created as today, the copy goes `ON_LOAN` and the Hold becomes `FULFILLED`. If the block or the loan limit refuses the checkout, the Hold stays `READY` and the copy stays on the Hold shelf.
+
+**Cancelling:**
+
+- An unknown id raises `HoldNotFound`.
+- A `FULFILLED`, `CANCELLED` or `EXPIRED` Hold raises `HoldNotAllowed`.
+- A `WAITING` Hold becomes `CANCELLED`.
+- A `READY` Hold becomes `CANCELLED`, and its copy passes on through the set-aside rule. The next Waiting Hold gets a deadline counted from today. If nobody is waiting, the copy goes back to `AVAILABLE`.
+- Cancelling has no money check and no charge.
+
+**The daily job (`expire_holds`):**
+
+- Every `READY` Hold whose Pickup deadline is before today becomes `EXPIRED`. Each one's copy then passes on through the set-aside rule, with deadlines counted from today.
+- A Hold made Ready during the run has a deadline at least 7 days away, so it can't expire in the same run.
+- The job returns the Holds it expired, in placement order. A second run on the same day returns `[]` and changes nothing.
+- The job works from today's date only. After missed days it expires everything now past its deadline.
+- Waiting Holds never expire. Expiry posts no Charge.
+
+**`holds_for`:** `TitleNotFound` for an unknown ISBN. Otherwise it returns the Title's `WAITING` and `READY` Holds in placement order. Placement order is the order the Holds were created, not `placed_on`, so Holds placed on the same day keep their order.
+
+**Unchanged:**
+
+- `withdraw_copy` still accepts only `AVAILABLE` copies, so a copy on the Hold shelf gets `CopyNotAvailable`.
+- `available_copies` still lists only `AVAILABLE` copies.
+- The overdue report, loan periods, due dates, loan limits, Fines, the Balance and the borrowing threshold.
+
+**Repository:** gains storage for Holds behind its existing style of interface: add a Hold, get one by id (raising `HoldNotFound`), and list Holds by Title and across all Titles in placement order. The service remains the only thing that changes state.
+
+**Docs:**
+
+- The README's Concepts section gains short entries for Hold, Hold queue, Hold shelf, Pickup deadline and Collect, consistent with `GLOSSARY.md`.
+- The README's Copy entry mentions `ON_HOLD_SHELF`.
+- The README's Blocked entry mentions the 5.00 hold threshold.
+
+## Testing Decisions
+
+- **One seam: the public `LendingService` interface**, built from the shared `service` and `clock` fixtures (`InMemoryRepository`, `FixedClock` starting Monday 2 March 2026). `conftest.py` stays unchanged.
+  - Queue tests use `dvd-1`: its only copy is `D1`, so checking it out means every copy is out.
+  - `978-1` (copies `B1`, `B2`) covers "a copy is still on the shelf" and "two copies, two Holds."
+  - Tests that need more members than `ann` and `kid` register them themselves.
+- **A good test** drives the service the way the desk would: `checkout`, `place_hold`, move the clock, `return_copy`, `add_copy`, `cancel_hold`, `expire_holds`. It asserts only on what the service returns or raises: the returned `Hold`s, `holds_for`, `get_copy(...).status`, `balance()` and the errors. Tests don't reach into the repository or call policy functions directly, so the queue storage and the deadline calculation can be refactored freely.
+- **Prior art:** the checkout/return tests, which use `clock.set(...)` and `clock.advance(...)` with explicit dates and `pytest.raises` for domain errors. The blocked-member tests show how to assert on `AccountBlocked`'s member, Balance and threshold.
+- **Behaviours to cover:**
+  - Placing a Hold when every copy is out gives a `WAITING` Hold, dated today, with no copy or deadline.
+  - `HoldNotAllowed` when:
+    - a copy is `AVAILABLE`;
+    - the Title has no copies;
+    - all of the Title's copies are withdrawn;
+    - the member already has a Waiting or a Ready Hold on the Title;
+    - the member has the Title on loan.
+  - A Hold is allowed when the only copies are on the Hold shelf for someone else.
+  - `AccountBlocked` from `place_hold` at exactly 5.00 and above, not at 4.99, carrying the member, Balance and 5.00. The same applies to a child.
+  - Check order for `place_hold`:
+    - unknown member gives `MemberNotFound`;
+    - a Blocked member with an unknown ISBN gives `AccountBlocked`;
+    - an unknown ISBN gives `TitleNotFound`.
+  - A return with someone waiting:
+    - the copy is `ON_HOLD_SHELF`;
+    - the first Hold is `READY` with that `copy_id` and the right deadline;
+    - later Holds stay `WAITING`;
+    - `return_copy` still returns the closed Loan;
+    - a late return still posts its Fine.
+  - A return with nobody waiting shelves the copy as before.
+  - Both deadline examples: Wednesday 4 → Wednesday 11 March, and Sunday 8 → Monday 16 March.
+  - Two copies coming back serve the first two Holds in placement order. The order holds for Holds placed on the same day.
+  - `add_copy` to a Title with a Waiting Hold sets the copy aside. With no Waiting Hold, it shelves it.
+  - Collecting:
+    - the Hold's member can check out the set-aside copy on the deadline day;
+    - the Hold becomes `FULFILLED`, the copy `ON_LOAN`, and it leaves `holds_for`;
+    - anyone else gets `CopyNotAvailable`;
+    - collecting after the deadline (before the job has run) gets `CopyNotAvailable`.
+  - A Hold member who owes 10.00 gets `AccountBlocked` at collection, and one at their loan limit gets `LoanLimitReached`. In both cases the Hold stays `READY`, and after paying (or returning) they can collect before the deadline.
+  - A Hold keeps its place after its member's Balance passes 5.00.
+  - Cancelling:
+    - a Waiting Hold is `CANCELLED` and leaves `holds_for`;
+    - a Ready Hold is `CANCELLED`, and its copy passes to the next Waiting Hold with a deadline from today, or goes back to `AVAILABLE` if nobody is waiting;
+    - a cancelled Ready Hold keeps its `copy_id` and `pickup_by`.
+  - `HoldNotAllowed` when cancelling a Fulfilled, Cancelled or Expired Hold. `HoldNotFound` for an unknown id.
+  - The job:
+    - nothing expires on the deadline day;
+    - the Hold expires the day after and is returned;
+    - its copy passes on with a deadline from that day, or goes `AVAILABLE`;
+    - a second run the same day returns `[]`;
+    - a run after several missed days expires everything past its deadline and passes copies on with deadlines from that day;
+    - Waiting Holds never expire;
+    - expiry leaves the Balance unchanged.
+  - `holds_for` lists Ready then Waiting Holds in placement order and excludes finished ones. It raises `TitleNotFound` for an unknown ISBN.
+  - `withdraw_copy` on a copy on the Hold shelf raises `CopyNotAvailable`. `available_copies` leaves it out.
+  - The existing tests pass unchanged.
+
+## Out of Scope
+
+- **Renewals**, the next feature. Rules already given:
+  - A Loan can't be renewed while its Title has any **Waiting** Hold. Ready Holds don't count, because those members already have their copy.
+  - Only members with a Balance of 0.00 when they ask can renew. Anything owed blocks renewal until it is paid.
+
+  Open questions for that feature:
+  - ADR-0001 requires renewing an overdue Loan to post the Fine built up so far. Is the Balance checked before that Fine is posted? "When they ask" suggests yes.
+  - Should a refusal for money reuse `AccountBlocked` with threshold 0.01, as Holds reuse it at 5.00?
+- **No-show fees** for uncollected Holds (a future kind of Charge; children exempt). Expiry is free for now.
+- A limit on how many Holds a member can have.
+- Expiring Waiting Holds, or letting a member say when they no longer need a Title.
+- Holds on a particular Copy, and Holds on Titles with no copies in circulation (for example, on order).
+- Telling members their Hold is Ready (notifications). Staff use `holds_for`.
+- Reordering a queue, staff priority, or pausing a Hold.
+- Listing a member's Holds, and any holds report.
+- Blocking members because they are holding overdue copies, as opposed to because of their Balance.
+- Persistence other than the in-memory repository.
+
+## Further Notes
+
+- **Collecting after the deadline before the job runs.** The glossary defines the Pickup deadline as the last day a Ready Hold can be collected. So `checkout` refuses a set-aside copy once its deadline has passed, even if `expire_holds` hasn't run yet. The Hold stays `READY` until the job expires it and passes the copy on. Confirmed with the user.
+- Children follow every hold rule exactly as adults do, including the 5.00 threshold.
+- ADR-0001 is untouched: setting a copy aside happens after the return's Fine is posted, and Holds never change the Balance.
+- All dates come from the injected Clock. Package code never calls `date.today()`.
