+# 03: Fines on late return
+
+**Spec:** `.scratch/overdue-fines/spec.md`
+
+**What to build:** Returning a copy late now costs the member money. `return_copy(copy_id)` keeps its signature and still returns the closed Loan. When the Loan was late, it also posts a Fine to the member's Account, dated on the return day and linked to the Loan.
+
+The Fine is the number of Late days times the material's daily rate: DVD 1.00, Book 0.25. Late days are the days after the due date, up to and including the return day, on which the library is open. The count uses the existing open-day rule in the circulation policy, not a hardcoded Sunday. The rates live in the circulation policy next to the loan periods.
+
+The Fines on one Loan together never exceed the Title's replacement cost. The Fine posted is therefore at most the replacement cost minus any Fines already on that Loan. Today a Loan has at most one Fine, but renewals will add more (see ADR-0001). Children are never fined. When the amount comes to zero, nothing is written.
+
+Fines are posted only when lateness ends (ADR-0001). An overdue copy still out on loan doesn't affect the Balance.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Account with Manual charges and Balance).
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] Book due Monday 23 March 2026 and returned Monday 30 March 2026: 6 Late days (Sunday 29 March excluded), so the Balance is 1.50.
+- [ ] DVD borrowed Monday 2 March and due Monday 9 March, returned Monday 16 March: 6 Late days (Sunday 15 March excluded), so the Balance is 6.00.
+- [ ] A return on the due date, or before it, posts no Fine.
+- [ ] A book due on a Saturday and returned the next day (Sunday) posts no Fine.
+- [ ] A very late DVD (replacement cost 12.00) gives a Balance of exactly 12.00. A very late book (18.00) gives exactly 18.00.
+- [ ] A child member's late return posts no Fine. The Loan is still closed and the copy shelved.
+- [ ] `return_copy` returns the same closed Loan as before, with `returned_on` set to the return day.
+- [ ] A member holding an overdue copy that hasn't come back still has a Balance of 0.00.
+- [ ] A Fine adds to existing Manual charges on the same Account.
+- [ ] The overdue report and its calendar-day `days_overdue` are unchanged, and its existing tests pass untouched.
+- [ ] Tests drive only the public `LendingService` interface with the shared fixtures and the `FixedClock`. They don't call policy functions directly.
+- [ ] The README Concepts section gains Fine and Late day, consistent with `GLOSSARY.md`.
+- [ ] All existing tests still pass.
