+# 04: Blocked members can't borrow
+
+**Spec:** `.scratch/overdue-fines/spec.md`
+
+**What to build:** A member who owes 10.00 or more can't take out another copy until they pay it down. `checkout` raises a new `AccountBlocked(LendingError)` when the member's Balance has reached the borrowing threshold of 10.00. The threshold is the same for every member category and lives in the circulation policy next to the loan limits. The error carries the member id, the Balance and the threshold it reached. It carries the threshold because a later hold feature will reuse it with its own lower threshold.
+
+The order of checks in `checkout` is: member lookup (`MemberNotFound`) first, then the block, then the existing copy lookup, availability and loan-limit checks in their current order. The money conversation therefore comes first. Paying the Balance below the threshold lets the member borrow again straight away.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Account with Manual charges and Balance), 02 (Payments).
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] `AccountBlocked(LendingError)` is added to the domain errors. It carries the member id, the Balance and the threshold, and has a readable message (for example "owes 12.00, limit 10.00").
+- [ ] With a Balance of exactly 10.00, `checkout` raises `AccountBlocked` and the copy stays available. A higher Balance is blocked too.
+- [ ] With a Balance of 9.99, `checkout` succeeds.
+- [ ] A Blocked member gets `AccountBlocked` rather than `CopyNotAvailable` when asking for a copy already on loan.
+- [ ] A Blocked member gets `AccountBlocked` rather than `LoanLimitReached` when already at their loan limit.
+- [ ] An unknown member still gets `MemberNotFound`.
+- [ ] A child can be Blocked through Manual charges, at the same 10.00 threshold.
+- [ ] After a Payment brings the Balance below 10.00, the same member can borrow again.
+- [ ] Tests drive only the public `LendingService` interface with the shared fixtures.
+- [ ] The README Concepts section gains Blocked, consistent with `GLOSSARY.md`.
+- [ ] All existing tests still pass.
