+# 03: Members who owe anything can't renew
+
+**Spec:** `.scratch/renewals/spec.md`
+
+**What to build:** Only a member whose Balance is 0.00 when they ask can renew. `renew` raises `AccountBlocked(member_id, balance, 0.01)` when the Balance is 0.01 or more. The renewal threshold is 0.01, the same for adults and children, and sits in policy next to the borrowing and hold thresholds.
+
+- The Balance is checked before any Fine for this renewal is posted. A member who owes 0.00 can renew an overdue book, even though the renewal then posts a Fine.
+- The check order becomes: returned, DVD, **owes money**, renewal limit, too early. A returned or DVD Loan is refused as such even when the member owes money. A member who owes money is told so even when the Loan is also at its limit or too early.
+- A refused renewal changes nothing, and posts no Fine.
+- The README's Blocked entry mentions the 0.01 renewal threshold.
+
+**Blocked by:** 02 (Only books, at most twice, from five days before the due date).
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] With a Balance of 0.01, `renew` raises `AccountBlocked` carrying the member, a Balance of 0.01 and a threshold of 0.01. The same happens with a larger Balance.
+- [ ] After paying back to 0.00, the same renewal goes through straight away.
+- [ ] A child who owes 0.01 is Blocked from renewing in the same way.
+- [ ] An adult who owes 0.00 renews an overdue book on Saturday 28 March: the renewal is granted and a Fine of 1.25 is posted. Their next renewal (inside the new window, from 13 April) raises `AccountBlocked` until they pay.
+- [ ] An overdue renewal refused because the member owes money posts no Fine, and the Balance is unchanged.
+- [ ] Check order:
+  - a returned Loan of a member who owes money raises `RenewalRefused`;
+  - a DVD Loan of a member who owes money raises `RenewalRefused`;
+  - a member who owes money gets `AccountBlocked` for a Loan already renewed twice, and for a request that is too early.
