+# 04: No renewal while someone is waiting for the Title
+
+**Spec:** `.scratch/renewals/spec.md`
+
+**What to build:** A Loan can't be renewed while its Title has a Waiting Hold, so members who are queueing get the next copy. `renew` raises `RenewalRefused`, with a `reason` naming the Hold, when any Hold on the Loan's Title is Waiting. Ready Holds don't count, because those members already have their copy on the Hold shelf.
+
+- This is the last check: returned, DVD, owes money, renewal limit, too early, **Waiting Hold**.
+- A refused renewal changes nothing. An overdue Loan refused this way posts no Fine.
+- Holds themselves are unchanged. A Hold placed after a renewal only stops the next renewal.
+
+**Blocked by:** 03 (Members who owe anything can't renew).
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] With both copies of `978-1` out (B1 and B2) and another member's Waiting Hold on the Title, renewing the Loan on B1 on Thursday 19 March raises `RenewalRefused`. The due date and `renewals` are unchanged.
+- [ ] Once B2 comes back and that Hold becomes Ready (with nobody else waiting), the same renewal goes through.
+- [ ] Once the Waiting Hold is cancelled, the renewal goes through.
+- [ ] An overdue Loan refused because of a Waiting Hold posts no Fine, and the Balance is unchanged.
+- [ ] Check order with a Waiting Hold on the Title:
+  - a member who owes money gets `AccountBlocked`;
+  - a Loan already renewed twice is refused for the limit;
+  - a request that is too early is refused as too early.
+- [ ] Tests drive only the public `LendingService` interface with the shared fixtures and the `FixedClock`. Tests that need a third member register one.
+- [ ] All existing tests, and those from tickets 01–03, still pass unchanged.
