new file mode 100644
index 0000000..078d96b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/GLOSSARY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+# Lending
+
+The circulation desk of the Elm Street public library: members, the catalogue, loans, and the money members owe for them.
+
+## Loans
+
+**Renewal**:
+Giving a Member a new due date on the Loan they already have, a full loan period from the day they renew, so the Loan keeps going as one Loan. Only books can be renewed: at most twice per Loan, no earlier than five days before the due date, and never while a Hold on the Title is Waiting.
+_Avoid_: Extension, re-checkout, re-issue
+
+## Accounts
+
+**Account**:
+The money side of a Member: every Charge and Payment recorded against them. Each Member has exactly one, from the day they register.
+_Avoid_: Member account, wallet, ledger
+
+**Charge**:
+An entry on an Account that increases what the Member owes. Fines and Manual charges are both kinds of Charge.
+_Avoid_: Debit
+
+**Fine**:
+A Charge for the Late days on a Loan, raised automatically when those Late days are settled, which today means when the copy comes back. All the Fines on one Loan together never exceed the Title's replacement cost. Child members are never fined.
+_Avoid_: Late fee, penalty, overdue charge
+
+**Manual charge**:
+A Charge that staff raise by hand, with a reason.
+_Avoid_: Staff charge, adjustment
+
+**Late day**:
+A day the library is open, falling after a Loan's due date up to and including the day the copy comes back. Days the library is closed are never Late days.
+_Avoid_: Overdue day (the overdue report counts calendar days, which is a different measure)
+
+**Payment**:
+Money a Member hands over, which reduces their Balance. A Payment is never assigned to particular Charges.
+_Avoid_: Credit, settlement
+
+**Balance**:
+What a Member owes right now: their Charges minus their Payments. It is never negative, and it does not include Fines still building up on copies not yet returned.
+_Avoid_: Debt, amount due, outstanding
+
+**Blocked**:
+The state of a Member whose Balance has reached the threshold for an action, such as borrowing. Each action has its own threshold.
+_Avoid_: Suspended, barred
+
+## Holds
+
+**Hold**:
+A Member's claim on the next copy of a Title that comes back, placed only when no copy of that Title is on the shelf. It is on the Title, never on a particular Copy. A Hold is Waiting until a copy is set aside for it, then Ready.
+_Avoid_: Reservation, request
+
+**Hold queue**:
+The Waiting and Ready Holds on one Title, in the order they were placed. A returned copy goes to the first Waiting Hold in it.
+_Avoid_: Waiting list, line
+
+**Hold shelf**:
+Where a returned copy is set aside for one Ready Hold until it is collected or the Pickup deadline passes.
+_Avoid_: Reserve shelf
+
+**Pickup deadline**:
+The last day a Ready Hold can be collected: seven days after it became Ready, moved to the next open day if the library is closed then.
+_Avoid_: Expiry date, hold-until date
+
+**Collect**:
+To check out the copy set aside for your own Ready Hold, which fulfils the Hold.
+_Avoid_: Pick up, claim
