+  for placing a Hold it is 5.00 and for renewing it is 0.01 (owing anything at
+  all), each the same for adults and children. `checkout` and `place_hold`
+  refuse a Blocked member with `AccountBlocked` (carrying the member id,
+  Balance and threshold) before looking at the copy or Title; `renew` does so
+  after the returned and DVD checks, and before posting any Fine for the
+  renewal itself. A Payment that brings the Balance below the threshold
+  unblocks them straight away. Fines still building up on copies not yet
+  returned don't count towards it.
+- **Hold** — a member's claim on the next copy of a Title that comes back
+  (`place_hold`). It is on the Title, never on a particular Copy, and can only
+  be placed when no copy of the Title is on the shelf. A Hold is refused with
+  `HoldNotAllowed` for a Title with no copies in circulation, or when the
+  member already has an active Hold on it or has it on loan. A Hold is
+  Waiting until a copy is set aside for it, then Ready. There is no limit on
+  how many Holds a member can have, and a member who becomes Blocked after
+  placing one keeps it.
+- **Hold queue** — the Waiting and Ready Holds on one Title, in the order they
+  were placed (`holds_for`), so Holds placed on the same day keep their order.
+  A returned or new copy goes to the first Waiting Hold in it.
+- **Hold shelf** — where a copy is set aside for one Ready Hold until
+  it is collected or the Pickup deadline passes. When a copy comes back
+  (`return_copy`) and someone is waiting for its Title, it goes to the Hold
+  shelf (`ON_HOLD_SHELF`) instead of the shelf, after any Fine is posted, and
+  the first Waiting Hold becomes Ready with that copy. With nobody waiting it
+  goes back on the shelf as `AVAILABLE`. A new copy (`add_copy`) is placed the
+  same way, so a Title never has a copy on the shelf while a Hold on it is
+  Waiting.
+- **Pickup deadline** — the last day a Ready Hold can be collected
+  (`pickup_by`): seven days after it became Ready, moved to the next open day
+  if the library is closed then, the same way due dates are. The daily job
+  (`expire_holds`) expires every Ready Hold whose deadline is before today and
+  returns them in placement order. Each copy passes to the next Waiting Hold,
+  with a deadline counted from the day the job runs, or goes back on the shelf.
+  Waiting Holds never expire, and expiry posts no Charge.
+- **Collect** — to check out the copy set aside for your own Ready Hold, which
+  fulfils the Hold. It is an ordinary `checkout`: the member gets a normal
+  Loan, the copy goes `ON_LOAN`, and the Hold becomes Fulfilled and leaves the
+  Hold queue, keeping its `copy_id` and `pickup_by`. Anyone else checking out
+  a copy on the Hold shelf, or the Hold's member after the Pickup deadline,
+  gets `CopyNotAvailable`. If the borrowing block or the loan limit refuses
+  the checkout, the Hold stays Ready and the copy stays on the Hold shelf, so
+  the member can pay or return something and still collect in time.
 
